   <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:ID="atom_chem_shift.ambiguity_code">
      <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="#atom_chem_shiftItem"/>
      <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="#atom_chem_shift"/>
      <rdfs:range>
         <owl:DataRange>
            <owl:oneOf>
               <rdf:List>
                  <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</rdf:first>
                  <rdf:rest>
                     <rdf:List>
                        <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</rdf:first>
                        <rdf:rest>
                           <rdf:List>
                              <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">3</rdf:first>
                              <rdf:rest>
                                 <rdf:List>
                                    <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">4</rdf:first>
                                    <rdf:rest>
                                       <rdf:List>
                                          <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">5</rdf:first>
                                          <rdf:rest>
                                             <rdf:List>
                                                <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">6</rdf:first>
                                                <rdf:rest>
                                                   <rdf:List>
                                                      <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">9</rdf:first>
                                                      <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
                                                   </rdf:List>
                                                </rdf:rest>
                                             </rdf:List>
                                          </rdf:rest>
                                       </rdf:List>
                                    </rdf:rest>
                                 </rdf:List>
                              </rdf:rest>
                           </rdf:List>
                        </rdf:rest>
                     </rdf:List>
                  </rdf:rest>
               </rdf:List>
            </owl:oneOf>
         </owl:DataRange>
      </rdfs:range>
      <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">

Ambiguity codes are used to define chemical shifts that have not been assigned
to specific atoms in the molecule studied.  Ambiguity in chemical shifts
may exist at several different levels, stereospecific ambiguity, intra and inter
residue ambiguities, etc.
                        </rdfs:comment>
      <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://bmrb.io/dictionary/tagdetail.php?tag=_Atom_chem_shift.Ambiguity_code"/>
   </owl:DatatypeProperty>
   <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:ID="atom_chem_shift.ambiguity_set_id">
      <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="#atom_chem_shiftItem"/>
      <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int"/>
      <rdfs:label>atom_chem_shift.ambiguity_set_id</rdfs:label>
      <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">

The ambiguity_set_ID defines those chemical shifts with ambiguity codes
of 4, 5, or 6 that form a known set of related chemical shift assignments.

1
                        </rdfs:comment>
      <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://bmrb.io/dictionary/tagdetail.php?tag=_Atom_chem_shift.Ambiguity_set_ID"/>
   </owl:DatatypeProperty>
